def derive(slice_, root=None, log_dir=None):
    """Measure one slice from ground truth. SIDE-EFFECT FREE. Never raises. Never dies.

    Returns a dict with exactly these keys:
        files_changed, prod_lines_added, prod_lines_deleted, test_lines_added,
        ears_criteria_count, skills_invoked      -> int or None
        quality_source                           -> one of QUALITY_SOURCES
        reason                                   -> "" when quality_source == "derived",
                                                    else a short non-empty slug naming the cause
                                                    (mr-record renders it as
                                                     `QUALITY(<source>): <reason>` in `notes`)

    RESOLUTION (plan R-E; never `git worktree list | grep`, whose unanchored match makes `lp-02`
    select an `lp-02b` worktree):
      * `root` defaults to HARNESS. TEST SEAM ONLY — the CLI never passes it.
      * Lock:      <root>/memory/projects/.harness-runner.<slice>.lock  (JSON as written by
                   mr-spawn: `repo`, `pr_repo`, `base_branch`, ...).
      * Worktree:  `worktree_path_for(lock, root)` — see its contract. Repo-keyed, mirroring
                   mr-launch.sh:29-31; None for an unsanitisable slice id.
      * Base:      the lock's `base_branch`, ALWAYS. The harness base is `main` and
                   monster-realm's is `master`; a hardcoded `main` would make every project slice
                   `unavailable` and leave N_MIN_SLICES satisfied by a biased subpopulation.
      * Pass log:  <log_dir or /tmp>/mr_pass_<slice>.log   (TEST SEAM, as above.)
      * Specs:     <root>/specs/monster-realm-v2/*.spec.md

    IDENTITY ASSERTION, NOT EXISTENCE (plan R-C — this is the whole point of the slice):
    `.claude/worktrees/` lives INSIDE the harness repo, so after the worktree is removed a
    `git -C <that path>` walks UP into the enclosing repo and returns rc 0 with an empty diff. Both
    an `isdir` check and a returncode check PASS there, yielding a confident, fabricated
    `files_changed=0, quality_source=derived` — and that is the NORMAL post-merge state, not an
    edge case (the worktree is deleted BEFORE the MERGED row is written). Therefore:
        git -C <p> rev-parse --show-toplevel   MUST equal the resolved worktree path, and
        the resolved path must be a real directory.
    Any mismatch -> ALL SIX columns None, quality_source "unavailable".

    STATES:
      * slice id failing SLICE_ID_RE (fullmatch)  -> all six None, "unavailable", NO path is
        constructed or touched, and no exception (64 real ledger rows carry ids that fail it,
        including one containing a path separator; mr-record:34 validates only non-emptiness).
      * lock missing / unreadable / identity mismatch / worktree absent -> all six None,
        "unavailable". `unavailable` is a ROW-LEVEL verdict: a row that mixed a measured
        `ears_criteria_count` with an unmeasurable diff would read as partially authoritative,
        which is exactly what `partial` exists to express (plan R-G).
      * `git status --porcelain` non-empty -> the FOUR diff columns None, quality_source
        "partial", and `ears_criteria_count`/`skills_invoked` still measured. CRASHED/PARKED rows
        are precisely the uncommitted-WIP case.
      * clean worktree, HEAD == merge-base -> a genuine 0/0/0/0, "derived".
      * otherwise -> "derived"; `ears_criteria_count` and `skills_invoked` are independently None
        when their source is absent, which does NOT downgrade quality_source.

    DIFF MEASUREMENT:
        base = git -C <p> merge-base <base_branch> HEAD
        git -C <p> --no-optional-locks diff --numstat -M <base> HEAD
      * `-M` is REQUIRED: without it a pure rename is two records and the counts silently double.
      * A binary record is `-<TAB>-<TAB>path`: it counts toward files_changed and contributes 0
        lines. NEVER int('-').
      * A rename record counts ONCE and is classified on the DESTINATION path.
      * files_changed counts every record including binary and OTHER; prod_lines_* sum PROD only;
        test_lines_added sums TEST only.

    SAFETY (plan R-D — the tick bumps its heartbeats BEFORE the reconcile and takes its flock 184
    lines later, so a stall here leaves the loop looking alive while it silently does nothing):
    list-argv only and NEVER a shell hop, read-only git subcommands only, never `fetch`,
    GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0, GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0, per-call timeouts, and every call routed through
    `_safe_run` below.
    """
    raise NotImplementedError(
        "lp-02 RED: derive() is not implemented — nothing measures files_changed / prod_lines_* / "
        "test_lines_added / ears_criteria_count / skills_invoked yet")


def variance(rows):
    """Read the new columns over a list of ledger row dicts and report. Returns (exit_code, lines).

    exit_code: 0 OK, 1 DEGENERATE, 2 INSUFFICIENT-DATA.  `lines` is a list of report strings.

    PIPELINE (plan R-F, which SUPERSEDES the original D6):
      1. Keep only rows where `is_closing(row["slice"], row["outcome"])`.
      2. FOLD to one observation per slice, preferring `quality_source == "derived"`. This is what
         makes ledger-replay statistically harmless and it is what the spec's phrase "slice-size
         denominator" actually asks for. `N_MIN_ROWS` is therefore redundant and was CUT.
      3. Per column, over the folded observations (a "null" is key-absent OR None):
             n_slices < N_MIN_SLICES  -> INSUFFICIENT-DATA        (exit 2, and NOT green)
             null_rate == 1.0         -> DEGENERATE all-null
             distinct(non-null) <= 1  -> DEGENERATE all-identical
             null_rate >= 0.5         -> DEGENERATE half-blind    (descends from the measured
                                                                   master_ci_after 65.8% empty)
             zero_rate >= 0.5         -> DEGENERATE silent-zero-suspect   (descends from A2; a
                                                                   systematically-zero column
                                                                   passes every null-based test)
      4. `master_ci_after` is EXCLUDED from the degeneracy ladder (the harness has no remote CI, so
         for harness slices it is permanently `not-applicable` and `distinct <= 1` would be a
         guaranteed false RED) and instead gets the hard R-B threshold: DEGENERATE when
         (unknown + not-recorded) / n_slices > 0.10.
      5. Overall: any DEGENERATE -> 1; else n_slices < N_MIN_SLICES -> 2; else 0.

    LINE CONTRACT (fixed, machine-checkable; the fixtures match on these tokens). `n_rows` counts
    the CLOSING rows that entered the fold; every other statistic — including the quality_source
    distribution and the unavailable rate — is computed over the FOLDED observations, so the two
    numbers together let a reader see that the fold happened:
        INFO n_rows=<int>
        INFO n_slices=<int>
        INFO quality_source derived=<n> replayed=<n> partial=<n> unavailable=<n> absent=<n>
        INFO unavailable_rate=<float>
